{"seconds": 397.6, "exit": 0, "final": "Confirmed the line is clean. Final answer:\n\n**Best move: Rg7+**\n\nThe pawn on e7 looks grabbable \u2014 two black rooks attack it \u2014 but it's also defended twice (Rd7 and Re1 down the open e-file). Any capture there (Rfxe7 or Rexe7) leads to a forced sequence of trades where White's second rook mops up the last black rook, winning a full piece. Since b7 is simply undefendable this move, the practical best try is Rg7+: a free check that gains a tempo, keeps the e8 rook anchored to block promotion, and avoids the e7 trap entirely. Lesson: before grabbing a \"hanging\" pawn, count attackers *and* defenders \u2014 if it's 2-vs-2, work out who recaptures last.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Rg7+\", \"line\": [\"Rg7+\", \"Kh5\", \"Kg8\", \"Rxb7\"], \"motifs\": [\"intermezzo\", \"hangingPiece\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "4r2k/pp1RPr2/2p5/2P5/1P4K1/P7/8/4R3 b - - 2 39"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "4r2k/pp1RPr2/2p5/2P5/1P4K1/P7/8/4R3 b - - 2 39"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "4r2k/pp1RPr2/2p5/2P5/1P4K1/P7/8/4R3 b - - 2 39"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "4r2k/pp1RPr2/2p5/2P5/1P4K1/P7/8/4R3 b - - 2 39", "move": "Rf4+"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "4r2k/pp1RPr2/2p5/2P5/1P4K1/P7/8/4R3 b - - 2 39", "move": "Rfxe7"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "4r2k/pp1RPr2/2p5/2P5/1P4K1/P7/8/4R3 b - - 2 39", "move": "Rexe7"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "4r2k/pp1Rr3/2p5/2P5/1P4K1/P7/8/4R3 w - - 0 40", "move": "Rdxe7"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "4r2k/pp1Rr3/2p5/2P5/1P4K1/P7/8/4R3 w - - 0 40", "move": "Rxb7"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "4r2k/pp2R3/2p5/2P5/1P4K1/P7/8/4R3 b - - 0 40", "move": "Rxe7"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "4r2k/pR2r3/2